[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-3cf27bae-13f8-431f-adff-b21e7c4e1f1f\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Track</p><strong>Thu 16 Apr 2026 14:30 - 14:45 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/icse-2026/icse-2026-venue-oceania-i\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Oceania I</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track#program\" class=\"navigate\">Analytics 3</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/maliizadi\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Mali Izadi</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"3cf27bae-13f8-431f-adff-b21e7c4e1f1f\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>A Comprehensive Study of Concurrency Bugs in the Linux Kernel</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><span class=\"pull-right\"><span title=\"Virtual Attendance\" class=\"output-badge\"><img alt=\"Virtual Attendance\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getImageFile/5a83481a-76b0-4d52-a281-ed633e8995d2/small?1776349051000\" class=\"outputimage\"/></span></span><p>Concurrency bugs, which arise from unexpected instruction orderings of concurrent execution contexts, are notoriously difficult to detect and diagnose due to their non-deterministic nature. Studies of concurrency bugs in user-space applications have shed light on common concurrency bug characteristics, informing the design of effective solutions for their detection, diagnosis, and repair. However, far less is known about concurrency bugs in operating system kernels, where low-level systems programming and complex execution patterns introduce new challenges. To address this gap, this paper presents the first comprehensive study of concurrency bugs in the Linux kernel.</p>\n<p>Our study reveals that kernel concurrency bugs exhibit surprisingly different characteristics compared to their counterparts in applications. For instance, 27.0% of kernel concurrency bugs only occur when certain interrupts are handled, which are rarely considered by existing bug discovery approaches. In addition, half of the bugs involve kernel driver code, but about 69.3% of these happen due to concurrent device operations on the control paths, such as device registration and deregistration, which suggests the driver control path should be a primary focus for concurrency bug discovery. Our findings reveal challenges and gaps in the existing approaches to finding kernel concurrency bugs. By shedding light on these challenges, this work paves the way for new operating system designs, testing tools, and verification efforts that will make modern operating systems more reliable and secure.</p>\n<p></p><a href=\"https://sishuaigong.github.io/pdf/icse26-concurrencybugstudy.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"publication-link navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-link\"></span> Pre-print</a><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/sishuaigong\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Sishuai Gong<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/chihenlin\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Chih-En Lin<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Purdue University</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/kevinwu2\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Kevin Wu<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Purdue University</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/edwinlu\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Edwin Lu<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Purdue University</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/pedrofonseca\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Pedro Fonseca<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Purdue University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/262/A-Comprehensive-Study-of-Concurrency-Bugs-in-the-Linux-Kernel\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-3cf27bae-13f8-431f-adff-b21e7c4e1f1f').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show');" },
